THE THREE ERROR-CHECK PRINCIPLES  (added 2026-08-08)
Cheap pre-flight tests. Each one killed a standing hypothesis this session
BEFORE implementation. Apply all three to any new statistic or constraint.
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

── I. THE ORBIT PRINCIPLE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
   Invariant theory: Cayley 1845, Gordan, Hilbert 1890 (basis theorem),
   EMMY NOETHER (1907 doctoral thesis, on invariants, under Gordan).
   Stated as a worldview by FELIX KLEIN, Erlangen Program 1872:
   "a property is geometric iff it is invariant under the group."

   Let a group G act on a set X. If s: X → S is G-INVARIANT, i.e.
   s(g·x) = s(x) for all g ∈ G, then s is CONSTANT ON EVERY G-ORBIT and
   therefore CANNOT DISTINGUISH two points in the same orbit.

   Proof: one line, definitional. Diagnostic power: total.

   TEST: what group leaves my statistic invariant, and does that group act
   transitively on the thing I am trying to separate?

   Instances found 2026-08-08:
     det(L_q) = N(q)²  — invariant under the norm-preserving group;
                         orbits are SPHERES; constant on them. Ratio
                         1.000000 verified. Killed the Phase 22 landmark.
     e₀ component      — every algebra automorphism fixes 1, so the
                         e₀-component is an Aut(𝕊)-INVARIANT. Blind by
                         construction to everything Aut can move. This is
                         why the census found 64% common mode: it is the
                         trivial representation.

   ⚠ THE DEEP FORM, and the reason this recurs in THIS framework:
   Noether's theorem says symmetry ⟹ conserved quantity. A conserved
   quantity conserves BECAUSE it does not change when things move. So the
   very property that makes an invariant physically meaningful makes it
   COMPUTATIONALLY BLIND to whatever the symmetry moves.
   THE SIGNAL IS NEVER IN THE INVARIANT. IT IS IN WHAT BREAKS THE SYMMETRY.
   (⟹ use the off-diagonal coupling block, the Assessor address, the
    angular quantities — never the norm, never det, never e₀.)

── II. THE DEGREES-OF-FREEDOM PRINCIPLE ───────────────────────────────────
   ROUCHÉ–CAPELLI theorem (also Kronecker–Capelli, Rouché–Frobenius).
   Counting form: DIRICHLET's pigeonhole (Schubfachprinzip, 1834).
   Nonlinear/general form: Krull dimension, Bézout.

   A linear system in n unknowns has solution space of dimension
   n − rank. More generally: a system with more unknowns than INDEPENDENT
   equations has a positive-dimensional solution set, and adding
   constraints OF THE SAME KIND does not reduce it.

   TEST: how many NEW unknowns does each new constraint introduce,
   relative to how many equations it supplies?

   Instance found 2026-08-08 — the digit window / Hensel lifting:
     each further digit of N supplies ONE congruence but introduces TWO
     unknowns (a digit of p AND a digit of q).
     After k digits: k equations, 2k unknowns, solution dim = k.
     Branching factor 10 per decimal digit, 2 per bit.
     10³⁰⁹ leaves = the brute-force count, UNCHANGED.

── III. THE IDEAL PRINCIPLE ───────────────────────────────────────────────
   HILBERT's NULLSTELLENSATZ (1893) and the ideal–variety correspondence.
   THE SHARPEST OF THE THREE. It explains the whole RSA dead end at once.

   The solution set of pq = N in the (p,q) plane is a variety V — a
   hyperbola. The polynomial functions vanishing on V are exactly the
   IDEAL ⟨pq − N⟩.

   EVERY constraint derived from N by algebraic manipulation LIES IN THAT
   IDEAL. By definition every element of the ideal VANISHES IDENTICALLY
   ON V. Therefore it excludes NOTHING. It adds ZERO rank.

   ⟹ You may derive infinitely many true statements from pq = N — last
     digits, mod-m relations, digit windows, size bounds — and every one
     of them is worth EXACTLY NOTHING, because they are all consequences
     of the one equation you already had.

   TEST — THE SINGLE MOST USEFUL QUESTION:
     IS MY CONSTRAINT DERIVABLE FROM N ALONE?
     If yes it is in the ideal, and it is worth nothing. To cut the
     variety you need information FROM OUTSIDE THE IDEAL.

   Every real attack imports outside information, and that is the ONLY
   thing they have in common:
     Coppersmith  — partial bits of p            (external)
     batch GCD    — a SECOND modulus             (external)
     ROCA         — structure in prime generation(external)
     timing/DPA   — side channel                 (external)
     Fermat       — the ASSUMPTION p ≈ q         (external, false for RSA)

   ⚠ NOT AN OBFUSCATION ADDED BY RSA'S DESIGNERS. The one-equation-in-
   two-unknowns structure is INTRINSIC TO MULTIPLICATION. Rivest, Shamir
   and Adleman did not build it — they SELECTED a problem that has it.

── THE OVERHEAD LADDER (why "linear reduction" can never arrive) ──────────
   constant factor   SIMD, GPU, wheel sieve   multiplies the constant only
   log factor        better data structures   shaves a log
   poly degree       n³ → n²                  still polynomial-land
   EXPONENT CLASS    exp(n) → exp(n^⅓)        ← GNFS did this, 1990s
   polynomial        exp(n^⅓) → n^k           NOT ACHIEVED classically

